# Design Foundations

The design foundations of Tuffex are grounded in three core axioms: **Physical Honesty**, **Sub-100ms Velocity**, and **Deterministic Discipline**.

It governs not merely raw CSS variables, but the physical geometric, material, and optical baselines of professional desktop interaction.

## Geometry & Squircles

### G2 Curvature Continuity & Squircles

Standard CSS `border-radius` relies on circular fillets ($G^1$ tangent continuity). Curvature $\kappa$ jumps abruptly from $0$ on straight edges to $1/R$ at the fillet boundary, inducing an optical crease (the Specular Break defect).

TuffEx draws superellipse (Lamé curve / squircle) corners on TxCard, TxModal, TxCommandPalette, TxFlipOverlay, the dialogs and CoreBox:
$$\left| \frac{x}{a} \right|^n + \left| \frac{y}{a} \right|^n = 1 \quad (n \approx 3.43)$$
The superellipse meets the straight edge with zero curvature ($G^2$ continuity) and cuts as deep along the 45° diagonal as the plain radius, so reflections run unbroken around the corner. The implementation is `tx-squircle` in `style/mixins.scss`; browsers without `corner-shape` keep the plain radius.

### Concentric Radii Geometric Law

When nested containers share the same numeric radius, the corner gap expands by $\sqrt{2}$ (approximately 1.414x), creating an ungrounded, pinched visual defect.
TuffEx enforces the geometric conservation law:
$$R_{\text{outer}} = R_{\text{inner}} + \text{Padding}$$

### Inset Clearance Against Caret Clipping

Corner curves encroach into content boxes. To prevent input carets from clipping into corner arcs, the horizontal inset must fully cover the radius:
$$Padding_{\text{horizontal}} \ge R$$
Single-line text containers apply a **0.65x golden optical padding ratio**, neutralizing the bottom-heavy illusion created by typographic leading.

## Surfaces & Refraction

### The Default to Refraction Mandate

All container components featuring a surface layer (modals, drawers, CoreBox panels, interactive cards) **must strictly default to `refraction`**.
Switching to `flat` or `mask` **mandates explicit manual user confirmation**.

### Snell's Refraction & RGB Dispersion Pipeline

`TxBaseSurface` leverages a GPU-accelerated SVG Displacement Map filter simulating Snell's Law as light traverses crystal prisms. Red, Green, and Blue channels carry asymmetric angular offsets, separating subtle spectral dispersion fringes along refracted contours.

### 120Hz Fallback & 140ms Elastic Recovery

During 120Hz window dragging, complex shaders **drop instantaneously (0ms) to an ultra-lightweight `mask`**, zeroing GPU load in one frame. Once motion ceases, the system applies **140ms damped recovery**, harmonizing material fidelity with smooth tracking.

## Color Science & Dark Palette

### #141414 Canvas & 3-Tier Elevation

Why reject pure black `#000000`?
1. **Preventing OLED Purple Smearing**: Switching OLED pixels off introduces latency, creating purple ghosting streaks when scrolling.
2. **Preserving Shadow Elevation**: Shadows must physically register darker than the background. `#141414` provides depth headroom for cast shadows.
3. **Three-Tier Elevation**: Canvas `--tx-bg-color: #141414`, Container `--tx-fill-color-blank: #1c1c1e`, Elevated `--tx-fill-color-light: #252528`.

### Dark Mode Retinal Bloom Weight Compensation

Under the Helmholtz optical irradiation effect, white strokes over dark canvases bleed into the retina, **reading bolder than the same weight in light mode**; how much depends on luminance, contrast and size, with no fixed percentage.
TuffEx does not lower weights in its dark theme today. When the font has a weight axis, a dark theme can tune its weights like this:
- Body copy: `400` (Light) $\to$ `380`–`400` (Dark)
- Inline emphasis: `500` (Light) $\to$ `460` (Dark)
- Headings: `600` (Light) $\to$ `560` (Dark)

### color-mix Ink Fusion & WCAG 4.5:1

Semantic text never uses isolated raw hues; it blends dynamically with primary ink:
`color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tx-color-danger) 55%, var(--tx-text-color-primary))`.
Contrast ratios consistently clear **4.58:1 – 4.81:1** across themes, ensuring strict WCAG 2.1 AA compliance.

## Typography & 13–14px Baseline

- **13px–14px Productivity Anchor**: Desktop productivity tools avoid oversized marketing typography, keeping crucial context within the human 2-degree foveal vision window.
- **Monospace 0.9em Optical Scale**: Code typefaces carry 15% taller x-heights; inline `<code>` scales to `0.9em` to preserve typographic line rhythm.
- **Modern Soft Line Breaks**: Long prose uses `text-wrap: pretty` to eliminate terminal orphans; short titles use `text-wrap: balance`; hardcoded `<br>` tags are banned.
- **Zero Tracking on Body Copy**: Modifying body `letter-spacing` destroys font kerning pairs and impairs reading velocity.

## Micro-Motion & Micro-Interactions

- **Motion as Spatial Anchors**: Micro-interactions resolve within **90ms–180ms**; animations must never block user keystrokes or clicks.
- **0ms Instant Hover**: Transitioning colors on `:hover` is banned (preventing sluggish lag); semantic shifts isolate transitions to `.is-morphing`.
- **90ms+90ms Confirmation Rhythm**: Menus apply a two-beat feedback rhythm (90ms clear highlight + 90ms active pulse) before closing.
- **Four Compositor Properties**: Confined strictly to `translate`, `scale`, `rotate`, and `opacity`; variables are banned in keyframes; dual alternating keyframe names eliminate reflow.

## AI Streaming & Anti-Jitter

- **useStreamPacer Cadence**: Releases units at 24ms intervals with a 600ms latency ceiling, smoothing network burstiness.
- **Twin-Layer Reserve Mirror**: Pre-measures full grid heights, eliminating stream height jitter and scrollbar twitching.
- **Immediate Text Selection & Copying**: Release tokens are standard DOM text nodes; users can drag-select and trigger `Cmd+C` at any millisecond without waiting.

